WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.892 --> 00:00:15.262
The children were drinking tea with Mr.

2
00:00:15.302 --> 00:00:17.164
Perks in the porter's room at the station.

3
00:00:18.185 --> 00:00:20.567
They had brought their own cups and some biscuits.

4
00:00:21.768 --> 00:00:26.352
Perks made tea in a beer can as usual, and everyone was happy and talkative.

5
00:00:26.372 --> 00:00:30.015
"When is your birthday, Mr.

6
00:00:30.055 --> 00:00:31.536
Perks?" Bobbie asked him.

7
00:00:32.708 --> 00:00:33.689
"My birthday?"

8
00:00:34.129 --> 00:00:34.669
asked Perks.

9
00:00:34.689 --> 00:00:38.391
"I gave up birthdays before you were born!"

10
00:00:38.411 --> 00:00:43.394
"But you must have been born at some time," said Phyllis thoughtfully.

11
00:00:43.414 --> 00:00:48.977
"Even if it was twenty years ago—or sixty or seventy!"

12
00:00:50.918 --> 00:00:52.659
"Not that long ago, missy!"

13
00:00:52.959 --> 00:00:54.160
Perks grinned as he answered.

14
00:00:54.180 --> 00:01:00.063
"Actually, I'll be 32 on the fifteenth of this month."

15
00:01:00.123 --> 00:01:01.284
Later the children talked.

16
00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:04.081
Perks was the best friend they had made.

17
00:01:05.201 --> 00:01:07.661
So they decided to do something special for his birthday.

18
00:01:10.642 --> 00:01:14.703
The next day at breakfast Mother smiled as she gave the children porridge and milk.

19
00:01:15.864 --> 00:01:20.185
"I've sold another story," she said, "so there'll be buns for tea."

20
00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:23.406
Phyllis, Bobbie, and Peter looked at each other.

21
00:01:24.526 --> 00:01:25.846
They were thinking the same thing.

22
00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:30.588
"Mother, can we have buns on the fifteenth instead?"

23
00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:31.488
Bobbie asked.

24
00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:35.402
"It's Perks' birthday, and we thought we'd have a small party."

25
00:01:35.422 --> 00:01:38.825
"Yes, you can," Mother replied.

26
00:01:38.845 --> 00:01:42.228
"We'll put his name on the buns with icing!"

27
00:01:43.109 --> 00:01:44.310
The children looked excited.

28
00:01:46.171 --> 00:01:49.113
Later Bobbie said, "I think we need flowers as well."

29
00:01:50.174 --> 00:01:52.536
"Yes, we need more ideas!

30
00:01:53.677 --> 00:01:56.740
Let's all be quiet and think," said Phyllis.

31
00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:59.922
"Hooray!" Peter cried suddenly.

32
00:02:01.383 --> 00:02:02.044
"I've got it!"

33
00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:03.289
He jumped up.

34
00:02:03.309 --> 00:02:06.571
"What?" said his sisters eagerly.

35
00:02:06.591 --> 00:02:10.994
"Well, Perks is so nice to everybody.

36
00:02:11.975 --> 00:02:15.737
There must be lots of people in the village who'd like to give presents to Perks.

37
00:02:16.838 --> 00:02:18.639
Let's go round and ask everyone."

38
00:02:18.659 --> 00:02:23.263
"Mother said we shouldn't ask people for things," said Bobbie doubtfully.

39
00:02:23.283 --> 00:02:28.687
"For ourselves, silly, not for other people," said Peter.

40
00:02:29.887 --> 00:02:30.428
So they went.

41
00:02:31.532 --> 00:02:34.454
The old lady at the post office didn't want to give Perks a present.

42
00:02:35.615 --> 00:02:39.819
"It's my birthday tomorrow and nobody cares about it," she said.

43
00:02:39.839 --> 00:02:43.382
"Why should I care about Perks' birthday?"

44
00:02:45.043 --> 00:02:46.845
The children left and went elsewhere.

45
00:02:47.965 --> 00:02:50.187
Some people were kind and some were not.

46
00:02:51.288 --> 00:02:54.491
At the end of the day, Peter wrote a list of things they'd received.

47
00:02:55.652 --> 00:02:58.274
He wrote it in the book where he kept the numbers of train engines.

48
00:03:00.055 --> 00:03:07.812
Presents Given: a pipe from the sweet shop some tea from the village store Presents Promised: some meat

49
00:03:07.852 --> 00:03:16.877
from the butcher six eggs from the farmer a spade from the blacksmith Early the next morning, Bobbie

50
00:03:16.917 --> 00:03:17.557
woke Phyllis.

51
00:03:18.678 --> 00:03:21.039
They had a plan but had not told Peter.

52
00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.240
He would think it was silly.

53
00:03:24.341 --> 00:03:27.603
They cut a bunch of roses and wrote a card: "For Mrs.

54
00:03:27.663 --> 00:03:29.384
Ransome, Happy Birthday."

55
00:03:31.936 --> 00:03:34.677
Bobbie and Phyllis took the roses and card to the post office.

56
00:03:35.978 --> 00:03:38.439
They put them on the counter before the old lady came in.

57
00:03:40.079 --> 00:03:44.481
When they got home, Peter was telling Mother about their plan to give Perks gifts for his birthday.

58
00:03:44.501 --> 00:03:49.043
"It depends on how you give him the presents," Mother said.

59
00:03:49.063 --> 00:03:53.345
"I hope he won't be offended and think it's charity.

60
00:03:54.405 --> 00:03:56.306
Poor people are very proud, you know."

61
00:03:56.326 --> 00:04:00.128
"It isn't because he's poor," said Phyllis.

62
00:04:01.332 --> 00:04:03.654
"It's because we like him very much."

63
00:04:05.495 --> 00:04:10.037
The morning of the fifteenth, the children watched Mother decorate the buns with pink icing.

64
00:04:11.838 --> 00:04:16.221
Then they went to the village to collect the spade and eggs and other things people had promised.

65
00:04:17.382 --> 00:04:19.303
They passed the old lady at the post office.

66
00:04:19.323 --> 00:04:23.525
"Thank you for the roses," she said.

67
00:04:23.545 --> 00:04:27.668
"Here, take these for Perks' birthday present."

68
00:04:28.936 --> 00:04:31.339
She brought out a basket full of red gooseberries.

69
00:04:31.359 --> 00:04:34.122
"And wait one more moment.

70
00:04:35.043 --> 00:04:36.825
I have something else for Perks!"

71
00:04:38.047 --> 00:04:39.008
The children smiled.

72
00:04:40.129 --> 00:04:42.271
Perks was going to have the best birthday ever!
